{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1513473076,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyODI2NjIxMjM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2038","origin":"github"},"title":"Support exporting multiple tarballs from a dataset","message":"#### What is the problem?\nMany online data hosting portals (zenodo, figshare, dataverse?) seems to not support datasets to have full hierarchy of directories, and provide only a \"flat list\" structure.  To avoid uploading 1 huge tarball, many datasets (e.g. [dataverse1](https://dataverse.harvard.edu/dataset.xhtml?persistentId=doi:10.7910/DVN/I7KP3V)) then are uploaded e.g. with each subject being a separate tarball.  In turn, we could export all top level files individually while uploading sub-directories as tarballs. This would be especially useful for incremental uploads where any particular subdataset is updated and remote hosting providing allowing for versioning of the files (e.g. figshare, dataverse)","files":null}]}